## Colour

| Role | Value | Use |
|------|-------|-----|
| Brand accent (warm apricot) | `#f0a05a` | Primary pills, waitlist band, selected chips, centre Log button |
| Range OK green | `#5fad6b` | In-range chart band, time-in-range bars, logo status dot when glucose is okay |
| Low glucose red | `#c8321f` light / `#ff7a6b` dark | Lows only, always with icon + text |
| Ink | `#14140f` | Headings, icons, dark fills |
| Body / muted | `#6e6e64` / `#919183` dark | Supporting copy |
| Canvas / tile / ash | `#ffffff` / `#f5f5eb` / `#d2d2c8` | Surfaces and rules |
| Dark island | `#14140f` / `#30302a` | Dark band, dark cards |

- Brand accent is never used as small text on white (too pale). Put it behind dark ink text.
- Range green is **semantic**, not decoration. Do not recolour the whole brand green.
- No second brand chromatic colour beyond apricot + the two clinical colours (range green, low red).

## Logo

- Wordmark `insulens` in Outfit/ink.
- A small range-OK green status dot next to or in the mark when glucose is in range (app chrome and marketing logo).
- When simulating low / out of range in the prototype, the status dot turns to the low-glucose red (still with text elsewhere).

## Typography

- **Outfit** for headings and every number (`tabular-nums`).
- **Albert Sans** for body, nav and buttons.
- Two-weight headlines: line 1 weight 600, soft line 2 weight 400 (can be muted).
- Sizes as before (h1 36→48, h2 30→36, body 16, etc.). Normal letter-spacing.

## Layout — dotted canvas + section boxes

- Full-bleed **dotted backdrop** is the page. Do **not** wrap the site in a Filament-style white bordered column with side gutters.
- Wide canvas (`max-w ≈ 1280px`) on the dotted backdrop — use the screen; do not crush into a tiny column.
- Sections are **soft rounded boxes** (`.surface-box`) with gaps so the dots show between them.
- Header: floating surface with cell rules, scrollspy active link, and a **small triangle** sitting on the bottom border of the active item (Filament cue).
- **Feature cards** (How it works, Privacy): corner L-brackets, icon in a disc, warm apricot hover lift — Insulens icons/colours, not Filament honey or 3D stock art.
- Hero: spacious text + live phone side by side on large screens.
- Dark / apricot islands (doctor, waitlist) are also rounded boxes on the same dotted canvas.

## Decorative SVG

- **None on the landing.** Do not add floating glucose waves, drops, sensor marks or other decorative SVG accents.
- Icons inside feature cards / UI chrome are fine (simple line icons tied to content). No stock art.

## Components

1. **Announcement tag:** dark chip with apricot accent glyph, e.g. "New › Doctor sharing".
2. **Hero:** two-weight headline, lead, apricot primary pill + soft secondary, live phone and SVG accents.
3. **Primary pill:** apricot fill, ink text, dark icon circle that expands on hover.
4. **Secondary pill:** parchment / charcoal fill, arrow nudge on hover.
5. **Feature cards:** rounded soft fill, simple icons (line or soft disc), no required corner brackets.
6. **Dark band:** one per page for product/demo context.
7. **Footer:** light, logo with status dot, links, back to top.

## Motion

- 200–300ms ease-out hovers. Scroll reveal once with light stagger.
- Pause looping animation offscreen; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- CSS or Motion. No GSAP.

## By surface

- **Landing:** warmer, more ownable than Filament; dotted canvas + section boxes; no decorative SVG accents; soft radii.
- **Phone app:** Apple + Strava structure (`.cursor/rules/app-style.mdc`). 28px cards. Brand apricot for primary actions; range green for in-range data and the logo status dot.

## Don't

- Don't clone Filament's layout chrome, honey/bubblegum colours, mascot or copy.
- Don't invent stats, testimonials, logos or clinical claims.
- No shadows, gradients-as-elevation, or neon lime.
- Don't use range green for every button — keep it meaningful for "glucose okay".
